00:45:12.920 --> 00:45:16.674
You know, the men who come
to this island, they're on the run.

524
00:45:16.800 --> 00:45:18.472
Hiding from the world.

525
00:45:19.120 --> 00:45:20.838
But not you.

526
00:45:21.480 --> 00:45:23.311
You're not here to hide.

527
00:45:24.120 --> 00:45:25.553
You're looking for someone.

528
00:45:29.680 --> 00:45:32.274
And who's to say
I haven't already found her?

529
00:45:37.480 --> 00:45:39.038
Was that meant to scare me?

530
00:45:39.160 --> 00:45:41.310
A little tremble would be nice.

531
00:45:42.640 --> 00:45:43.834
Well,

532
00:45:44.640 --> 00:45:47.757
considering you're one tremble away
from limping out of here...

533
00:45:50.680 --> 00:45:52.318
...I'd say I'm close enough.

534
00:45:53.080 --> 00:45:54.296
Does this mean you're not making me

535
00:45:54.320 --> 00:45:55.514
breakfast in the morning?

536
00:45:59.120 --> 00:46:01.190
I'd say you're a couple inches off.

537
00:46:07.360 --> 00:46:08.918
Bit of a stalemate.

538
00:46:09.040 --> 00:46:10.917
Not if you drop the gun.

539
00:46:11.080 --> 00:46:13.196
I'm not the bad guy.

540
00:46:14.680 --> 00:46:16.955
I don't believe in good guys.

541
00:46:17.680 --> 00:46:19.033
Serena?

542
00:46:22.040 --> 00:46:23.951
Who's your friend?

543
00:46:24.800 --> 00:46:26.597
We just met.

544
00:46:27.120 --> 00:46:30.430
But we were getting along
famously until somebody

545
00:46:31.040 --> 00:46:32.871
decided to interrupt.

546
00:46:33.160 --> 00:46:34.434
Stick to the path.

547
00:46:35.240 --> 00:46:36.355
Here, honey.

548
00:46:36.480 --> 00:46:39.631
There's a lot of
unmarked graves on the island.

549
00:46:42.720 --> 00:46:45.393
I'll bet whoever sold you that shirt
is in one of them.

550
00:46:46.720 --> 00:46:48.870
And how long do you intend to
push your luck?

551
00:46:49.680 --> 00:46:51.318
Until I get what I came for.

552
00:46:52.040 --> 00:46:53.393
Which is what exactly?

553
00:46:56.320 --> 00:46:57.753
A damn,

554
00:46:57.760 --> 00:46:59.478
A damn, strong drink.

555
00:47:22.760 --> 00:47:26.548
So, let's be real and talk about
what we all really want.

556
00:47:34.120 --> 00:47:35.758
I'm only here for that.

557
00:47:36.520 --> 00:47:38.715
And in my mind,
you guys could walk away nicely.

558
00:47:38.880 --> 00:47:40.632
Unless you want to
continue our foreplay.

559
00:47:41.720 --> 00:47:43.950
Power like that doesn't belong
in anyone's hands.

560
00:47:46.080 --> 00:47:47.513
Just improvising.

561
00:47:56.120 --> 00:47:57.917
Mate, seriously? A grenade?

562
00:47:58.000 --> 00:47:59.736
What is this?
Eastern Europe in the early '90s?

563
00:47:59.760 --> 00:48:01.079
Next, he's gonna send you a fax.

564
00:48:02.640 --> 00:48:03.959
So, you're willing to kill

565
00:48:05.000 --> 00:48:06.956
just to keep that for yourself?

566
00:48:07.080 --> 00:48:08.718
That's the wrong question to ask.

567
00:48:09.760 --> 00:48:10.800
What's the right question?

568
00:48:14.400 --> 00:48:15.680
"Are you willing to die for it?"

569
00:48:21.760 --> 00:48:24.149
One grenade, three people.

570
00:48:24.280 --> 00:48:25.679
I like the odds.

571
00:48:31.800 --> 00:48:34.439
Two grenades, three people.

572
00:48:35.000 --> 00:48:37.355
I'm loving these odds.

573
00:48:41.720 --> 00:48:43.153
You ever bleed so much,

574
00:48:43.240 --> 00:48:45.310
when you open your eyes,
all you see is red?

575
00:48:45.480 --> 00:48:48.552
When you have fought war
on every continent...

576
00:48:48.640 --> 00:48:50.437
Come on, X, just say the word.

577
00:48:50.520 --> 00:48:52.909
Let me put both these assholes
out to pasture.

578
00:48:53.000 --> 00:48:54.274
...you expect death.

579
00:48:54.360 --> 00:48:56.396
Our bodies are such fragile things.

580
00:48:56.520 --> 00:48:57.560
Come on. Let me shoot him.

581
00:48:58.520 --> 00:48:59.555
Death sometimes just

582
00:49:00.520 --> 00:49:01.669
sneaks up on you.

583
00:49:03.520 --> 00:49:05.520
It's been a while
since I played hot potato.

584
00:49:06.880 --> 00:49:08.598
I'm in this hospital bed.

585
00:49:08.680 --> 00:49:10.272
I'm barely conscious. Delirious.

586
00:49:10.360 --> 00:49:12.590
Drowning in my own blood.

587
00:49:12.720 --> 00:49:16.235
And all I can hear myself think is,
"Today's the day."

588
00:49:16.320 --> 00:49:17.992
"Today's the day you die."

589
00:49:19.320 --> 00:49:20.753
I'm touched.

590
00:49:20.840 --> 00:49:23.354
Can I have my jacket,
when you get a sec?

591
00:49:23.480 --> 00:49:25.040
Then a man comes along,
tells me a story

592
00:49:25.680 --> 00:49:28.353
about a drought in California.

593
00:49:29.360 --> 00:49:31.351
About skateboards
and swimming pools.

594
00:49:32.880 --> 00:49:35.030
About a man named Xander Cage.

595
00:49:35.640 --> 00:49:37.870
Oh, shit. He's Triple-X.

596
00:49:42.400 --> 00:49:43.719
I heard he was dead.

597
00:49:46.640 --> 00:49:47.640
Is he?

598
00:49:51.080 --> 00:49:53.071
We are all Triple-X.

599
00:49:54.200 --> 00:49:56.191
We just have different agendas.

600
00:49:56.840 --> 00:49:58.398
She wants to destroy it.

601
00:49:59.640 --> 00:50:00.868
I'm gonna use it.

602
00:50:02.320 --> 00:50:06.029
And I'll be damned if I'm gonna let you
take it back to the NSA.

603
00:50:08.920 --> 00:50:11.115
I don't want a lover

604
00:50:13.080 --> 00:50:15.116
I just need a friend

605
00:50:28.760 --> 00:50:29.954
Now, it's a party.

606
00:50:47.360 --> 00:50:50.079
Everybody, get down! Move! Move!

607
00:50:50.200 --> 00:50:52.236
Shit's about to go down.

608
00:50:52.880 --> 00:50:53.995
You ready to have some fun?

609
00:50:55.320 --> 00:50:57.276
Turn the music off!

610
00:50:57.440 --> 00:50:58.509
Stop it!

611
00:51:07.960 --> 00:51:09.712
Everybody, hands up!

612
00:51:09.800 --> 00:51:10.800
Now!

613
00:51:12.040 --> 00:51:13.359
On the floor!

614
00:51:14.360 --> 00:51:17.352
First person to move,
first person to die!

615
00:51:24.680 --> 00:51:25.680
I moved.

616
00:51:31.520 --> 00:51:35.149
I just moved again.
I'm still alive.

617
00:51:35.320 --> 00:51:36.912
Shut up, "hero"!

618
00:51:37.680 --> 00:51:39.079
All right.

619
00:51:39.760 --> 00:51:41.239
Let's do this.

620
00:51:41.360 --> 00:51:42.713
Don't move!

621
00:51:45.680 --> 00:51:48.672
Okay, I actually have what you want.

622
00:51:48.800 --> 00:51:50.836
Pandora's Box?

623
00:51:51.480 --> 00:51:53.436
I got it right here.

624
00:51:53.520 --> 00:51:55.431
But you're wrong, though.

625
00:51:55.520 --> 00:51:58.990
You take it from me, and you die first.

626
00:51:59.080 --> 00:52:02.277
Then Lieutenant Leningrad,
who thinks he's got your back.

627
00:52:03.200 --> 00:52:04.474
Then the two Ivans by the door.

628
00:52:05.040 --> 00:52:07.554
Moscow Mule by the bar.

629
00:52:08.440 --> 00:52:11.477
And then Igor on the stairs.

630
00:52:12.120 --> 00:52:13.951
See where we're going with this?

631
00:52:16.120 --> 00:52:17.394
But none of that matters.

632
00:52:18.400 --> 00:52:19.549
'Cause like I said,

633
00:52:21.080 --> 00:52:25.153
if you take this from me, you die first.

634
00:52:26.080 --> 00:52:28.150
I'll take it from you dead or alive.

635
00:52:30.120 --> 00:52:34.557
And if you hold it too tight,
I cut your arm off.

636
00:52:34.720 --> 00:52:36.073
Suit yourself.

637
00:52:45.800 --> 00:52:46.800
Leningrad.

638
00:52:47.080 --> 00:52:48.229
Hi, Ivan.

639
00:52:48.680 --> 00:52:49.680
Other Ivan.

640
00:52:52.400 --> 00:52:53.435
Whoo!

641
00:52:59.920 --> 00:53:01.069
Ooh, bye-bye, Moscow Mule.

642
00:53:06.720 --> 00:53:08.517
Igor. That's another one you owe me, X.

643
00:53:09.120 --> 00:53:10.917
Read between the lines.

644
00:53:28.640 --> 00:53:30.392
Tennyson!
Some back-up would be nice.

645
00:53:30.480 --> 00:53:32.391
- Huh?
- Some back-up would be nice!

646
00:53:32.520 --> 00:53:33.794
Come on, man!

647
00:53:33.880 --> 00:53:35.552
X said stay on the boat.

648
00:53:39.800 --> 00:53:42.280
That was before the goddamn
Russian invasion touched down, man!

649
00:55:18.080 --> 00:55:19.718
X said stay on the boat.

650
00:55:36.360 --> 00:55:37.554
You want to play?

651
00:57:19.520 --> 00:57:21.476
That doesn't belong in anyone's hands.

652
00:57:22.320 --> 00:57:25.312
You want it, come and get it.

653
00:57:29.560 --> 00:57:30.879
Was that necessary?

654
00:57:31.400 --> 00:57:33.834
It's what Gibbons would have wanted.

655
00:57:38.880 --> 00:57:39.880
X!

656
00:57:42.400 --> 00:57:43.400
X.

657
00:57:43.560 --> 00:57:46.518
It happened again. Another satellite fell.

658
00:57:49.760 --> 00:57:52.672
Us working as a team.

659
00:57:53.040 --> 00:57:54.519
That's what Gibbons would've wanted.

660
00:57:57.960 --> 00:57:59.552
You in?

661
00:57:59.680 --> 00:58:04.071
An explosion inside
the Olympic Stadium rocks Moscow.

662
00:58:04.160 --> 00:58:06.071
Seven workers are now confirmed dead,

663
00:58:06.160 --> 00:58:08.196
with at least 25 others injured

664
00:58:08.280 --> 00:58:10.236
in this senseless act of violence.

665
00:58:10.360 --> 00:58:12.590
A source inside the Pentagon

666
00:58:12.720 --> 00:58:16.872
says a rogue satellite
may have been used as a weapon.

667
00:58:17.160 --> 00:58:20.835
Guess this means Pandora's Box
isn't exactly classified.

668
00:58:21.120 --> 00:58:23.315
In a new video released
just moments ago,

669
00:58:23.400 --> 00:58:24.594
an anonymous group

670
00:58:24.680 --> 00:58:28.434
is claiming to have the ability
to use satellites as weapons.

671
00:58:28.520 --> 00:58:31.876
They claim "that
the violation of civil liberties

672
00:58:31.960 --> 00:58:33.712
"of all the citizens of the world

673
00:58:33.800 --> 00:58:36.234
"is an atrocity that must be stopped."

674
00:58:36.360 --> 00:58:39.376
Disable and
dismantle all the world's spy programs

675
00:58:39.400 --> 00:58:42.278
within the next 24 hours,

676
00:58:42.400 --> 00:58:44.914
or I'll do it for you,
one satellite at a time.

677
00:58:45.040 --> 00:58:48.032
There are 30,000 satellites
orbiting the Earth at this moment.

678
00:58:48.160 --> 00:58:52.756
I will drop one satellite every 24 hours
until my demands are met.

679
00:58:52.920 --> 00:58:54.672
Eyewitnesses in Moscow...

680
00:58:54.800 --> 00:58:56.416
Was this always part of
your mission, too?

681
00:58:56.440 --> 00:58:57.440
Of course not.

682
00:58:59.160 --> 00:59:02.072
We were a new T riple-X team
Gibbons created.

683
00:59:02.160 --> 00:59:04.390
We discovered
a high-level intelligence officer

684
00:59:04.480 --> 00:59:06.516
was trying to manipulate satellites.

685
00:59:06.840 --> 00:59:09.752
And even before we could unmask him,

686
00:59:09.840 --> 00:59:11.353
Gibbons was killed.

687
00:59:11.520 --> 00:59:13.636
So, you knew they were
Triple-X all along.

688
00:59:13.760 --> 00:59:15.990
I needed you to retain
a sense of objectivity.

689
00:59:16.560 --> 00:59:18.790
I don't understand.
If I destroyed Pandora's Box,

690
00:59:18.920 --> 00:59:20.592
what happened in Moscow?

691
00:59:20.680 --> 00:59:22.591
If I'm right, which I am,

692
00:59:22.720 --> 00:59:24.080
this box only ever had the ability

693
00:59:24.120 --> 00:59:26.270
to control one satellite.

694
00:59:26.400 --> 00:59:27.674
What does that mean?

695
00:59:27.800 --> 00:59:30.360
It means
we've been chasing a prototype.

696
00:59:31.120 --> 00:59:32.256
And these guys have the real one?

697
00:59:32.280 --> 00:59:33.280
Yeah.

698
00:59:42.840 --> 00:59:44.831
Serena played us for fools.

699
00:59:46.160 --> 00:59:47.434
Betrayed us.

700
00:59:48.160 --> 00:59:49.718
This isn't about Serena.

701
00:59:49.800 --> 00:59:51.313
This is war. And either

702
00:59:51.440 --> 00:59:54.352
we stop it today,
or we watch the world burn tomorrow.

703
00:59:54.440 --> 00:59:56.351
- Can't lose focus on that.
- Yeah.

704
00:59:57.920 --> 00:59:59.114
Where you been?

705
00:59:59.280 --> 01:00:00.998
You stop off for the old rub-and-tug?

706
01:00:01.200 --> 01:00:02.235
Your mom says hi.

707
01:00:03.520 --> 01:00:05.636
Tracker on board? Nobody saw you?

708
01:00:05.760 --> 01:00:07.671
- Nobody ever sees me, boss.
- Good.

709
01:00:08.440 --> 01:00:12.274
Now, these suits control
every spy satellite in the sky.

710
01:00:12.400 --> 01:00:16.712
But how often do these seven men
all sit in the same room together?

711
01:00:17.280 --> 01:00:18.429
Almost never.

712
01:00:18.560 --> 01:00:21.438
And if you needed
retinal scans,

713
01:00:21.520 --> 01:00:22.520
cell phone data dumps,

714
01:00:22.680 --> 01:00:25.672
biometrics of all
the superpowers in the world,

715
01:00:27.320 --> 01:00:29.390
who would you target?

716
01:00:29.520 --> 01:00:30.520
Oh, shit.

717
01:00:30.640 --> 01:00:34.269
Who has that kind of power
to actually set that in motion?

718
01:00:34.400 --> 01:00:37.153
Oh, you're pissing up
the wrong tree, Cage.

719
01:00:37.240 --> 01:00:39.151
I came looking for you, remember?

720
01:00:39.280 --> 01:00:42.272
Yo, asshole. We gonna have problems?

721
01:00:42.400 --> 01:00:45.119
Oh, no problem. How was your trip?

722
01:00:45.280 --> 01:00:47.874
I'm just doing the math.

723
01:00:48.160 --> 01:00:50.230
Oh, yeah? What math?

724
01:00:50.560 --> 01:00:53.757
Air velocity divided by distance.

725
01:00:53.920 --> 01:00:56.229
So, when I stuff you down the toilet,

726
01:00:56.720 --> 01:00:58.153
search and rescue will know where

727
01:00:58.240 --> 01:01:00.470
to find you between China
and North Korea.

728
01:01:00.560 --> 01:01:02.073
Keep talking shit, little man.

729
01:01:02.200 --> 01:01:04.316
Hold that thought, G.I.Joe.

730
01:01:05.080 --> 01:01:06.229
Wow.

731
01:01:06.760 --> 01:01:08.079
Roll it back.

732
01:01:09.200 --> 01:01:10.553
A little more.

733
01:01:10.640 --> 01:01:11.640
More.

734
01:01:12.960 --> 01:01:15.315
A little more. Stop.

735
01:01:15.440 --> 01:01:18.113
Okay, when Xiang broke the window,

736
01:01:22.600 --> 01:01:24.272
he's the only one that didn't flinch.

737
01:01:26.520 --> 01:01:27.960
I need the President on the phone...

738
01:01:28.120 --> 01:01:29.736
That's not gonna come off,
you know that, right?

739
01:01:29.760 --> 01:01:31.990
I'll have to replace
the goddamn screen.

740
01:01:32.120 --> 01:01:33.456
I've been saying the director of the CIA

741
01:01:33.480 --> 01:01:35.755
has been trying
to destroy the world for years.

742
01:01:35.840 --> 01:01:39.435
Okay, we have carte blanche to track
this son of a bitch down.

743
01:01:39.800 --> 01:01:42.189
Do any of you know how to do it?

744
01:01:42.520 --> 01:01:45.080
The same way Xiang and I found
Pandora's Box in New York.

745
01:01:48.480 --> 01:01:50.136
Pandora's Box needs to
keep reconnecting itself

746
01:01:50.160 --> 01:01:52.037
because the satellites orbit.

747
01:01:52.120 --> 01:01:54.031
- Excuse me.
- Uh.

748
01:01:54.240 --> 01:01:56.993
All we need to do is
track down the main signal,

749
01:01:57.080 --> 01:01:59.799
and then we can approximate
its location within a 20-mile radius.

750
01:02:05.240 --> 01:02:07.549
Of all the places
in the world to lay low,

751
01:02:08.040 --> 01:02:09.871
this fruit loop chooses Detroit?

752
01:02:17.640 --> 01:02:19.720
These blasts did take place in Moscow,

753
01:02:19.840 --> 01:02:21.910
but they were felt around the world.

754
01:02:22.000 --> 01:02:26.551
Good morning. As feared, the death toll
in the Moscow tragedy is rising.

755
01:02:26.680 --> 01:02:28.159
In addition to the latest deaths...

756
01:02:28.240 --> 01:02:30.674
Let me guess.
Everyone's jumping at the chance

757
01:02:30.760 --> 01:02:32.830
to dismantle their spy programs.

758
01:02:33.840 --> 01:02:35.398
No.

759
01:02:35.520 --> 01:02:39.308
The world's too stupid to realize
that Moscow wasn't a bluff.

760
01:02:43.040 --> 01:02:43.950
Okay, Triple-X,

761
01:02:44.040 --> 01:02:46.156
you will base out of
an NSA safe house.

762
01:02:46.280 --> 01:02:48.794
Becky will coordinate
earbud communications

763
01:02:48.880 --> 01:02:51.110
and have the signal disruptor
on standby.

764
01:02:51.200 --> 01:02:54.636
Nicks, when I crashed the boat up
on shore and saved your life...

765
01:02:55.040 --> 01:02:56.359
Yeah, whatever, bro.

766
01:02:56.600 --> 01:03:00.115
...do you think that counts
as crash 199 for me?

767
01:03:00.200 --> 01:03:01.952
You know, officially?

768
01:03:02.040 --> 01:03:03.792
Officially, you're deranged.

769
01:03:06.520 --> 01:03:07.520
Cool.

770
01:03:07.720 --> 01:03:10.640
We'll set up a triangulated
signal tracking system around the city.

771
01:03:11.280 --> 01:03:13.714
And when
Becky locks in his exact location,

772
01:03:13.800 --> 01:03:14.869
we make our move.

773
01:03:15.360 --> 01:03:18.796
What about you?
How did you get roped into all this?

774
01:03:18.880 --> 01:03:22.270
I tagged a skyscraper
and got a year in jail for it.

775
01:03:22.400 --> 01:03:23.628
Jail?

776
01:03:25.120 --> 01:03:26.792
- Seems excessive.
- Mmm-hmm.

777
01:03:27.240 --> 01:03:29.470
The tag was 30 stories tall.

778
01:03:30.160 --> 01:03:32.037
Two million hits on YouTube.

779
01:03:32.200 --> 01:03:34.475
And I served only half the sentence.

780
01:03:34.560 --> 01:03:37.438
Let me guess. Gibbons to the rescue.

781
01:03:37.560 --> 01:03:39.391
Yup. He said a lion like me

782
01:03:39.480 --> 01:03:40.880
doesn't belong in any kind of cage.

783
01:03:48.760 --> 01:03:52.355
I got mine after I left the NSA.

784
01:03:52.920 --> 01:03:54.136
What about that one on your wrist?

785
01:03:54.160 --> 01:03:55.479
London.

786
01:03:55.640 --> 01:03:58.916
2009. I climbed the Millennium Wheel.

787
01:03:59.760 --> 01:04:00.760
Naked.

788
01:04:00.840 --> 01:04:02.432
- Naked?
- Yeah.

789
01:04:02.960 --> 01:04:04.439
High school.

790
01:04:06.080 --> 01:04:07.991
Oh, no!

791
01:04:08.080 --> 01:04:10.992
We all have our
embarrassing moments.

792
01:04:14.440 --> 01:04:16.476
What about that sexy one?

793
01:04:16.600 --> 01:04:19.433
This?
Phoenix out of the ashes.

794
01:04:19.760 --> 01:04:21.955
Eighteen hours in a chair in Mexico.

795
01:04:22.120 --> 01:04:24.156
I drank my bodyweight in tequila
to get through it.

796
01:04:25.760 --> 01:04:27.591
It's the most important one, actually.

797
01:04:29.120 --> 01:04:32.430
It's when I decided to change the world
instead of

798
01:04:32.960 --> 01:04:34.279
rage against it.

799
01:04:39.440 --> 01:04:41.829
We found him.
We found Pandora's Box.

800
01:04:43.000 --> 01:04:44.956
Xander, do you copy?

801
01:04:45.120 --> 01:04:47.998
We're here.
Okay, send Tennyson.

802
01:04:48.120 --> 01:04:50.634
Uh, looks like East 404 Congress Street.

803
01:04:50.720 --> 01:04:51.720
He's on the top floor.

804
01:05:02.400 --> 01:05:05.198
I'm showing activity in Pandora's Box.
I can jam the signal,

805
01:05:05.320 --> 01:05:08.357
but only for a few minutes, so hurry.

806
01:05:11.760 --> 01:05:14.080
You've got to get there fast
and take this guy down.

807
01:05:18.080 --> 01:05:20.310
Not if we find him first.

808
01:05:27.280 --> 01:05:28.800
Whoa! Red light! Red light! Red light!

809
01:05:31.920 --> 01:05:32.989
Whoo!

810
01:05:34.200 --> 01:05:36.280
Did you know traffic signals
were invented by Big Oil

811
01:05:36.360 --> 01:05:38.271
to waste fuel and drive up profits?

812
01:05:38.360 --> 01:05:40.590
If I say yes, will you please
just slow down? Look out!

813
01:05:43.600 --> 01:05:44.600
Wait.

814
01:05:44.680 --> 01:05:47.274
Is this the part where you act
the basic bitch

815
01:05:47.360 --> 01:05:48.496
and tell me you got your eye on me

816
01:05:48.520 --> 01:05:49.616
and that you don't trust me?

817
01:05:49.640 --> 01:05:51.676
- Welcome to the moment.
- Whoa, whoa, whoa

818
01:06:05.360 --> 01:06:06.713
Everyone needs backup.

819
01:06:10.720 --> 01:06:12.039
Stop, stop, stop, stop!

820
01:06:12.160 --> 01:06:13.309
Stop, stop, stop, stop!

821
01:06:18.160 --> 01:06:19.229
Tennyson?

822
01:06:21.400 --> 01:06:22.958
Gridlocked.

823
01:06:23.560 --> 01:06:24.595
There it is.

824
01:06:26.360 --> 01:06:28.316
If you run into trouble,

825
01:06:28.880 --> 01:06:30.199
dial nine.

826
01:06:30.720 --> 01:06:32.358
It's an old Gibbons fail-safe.

827
01:06:47.960 --> 01:06:50.474
You crashed my party!
Stole my dance partner.

828
01:06:51.440 --> 01:06:52.759
I'm gonna crash yours.

829
01:06:52.840 --> 01:06:53.909
Have fun.

830
01:06:54.040 --> 01:06:56.759
This ain't a party. This is a race.

831
01:07:10.480 --> 01:07:12.198
What the hell you think you're doing?

832
01:07:12.280 --> 01:07:13.349
Building a ramp.

833
01:07:24.200 --> 01:07:25.553
Go, go, go!

834
01:07:57.640 --> 01:07:59.119
Go, go, go, go!

835
01:08:06.160 --> 01:08:08.240
- Hey! Out of the car! Get out!
- What are you doing?

836
01:08:08.320 --> 01:08:09.673
Let's go!

837
01:08:52.840 --> 01:08:53.840
Wow.

838
01:09:12.560 --> 01:09:14.471
Shit. He's trying to reconnect it.

839
01:09:14.600 --> 01:09:16.636
Guys, I can only
jam the signal for so long

840
01:09:16.720 --> 01:09:17.816
before he chooses another satellite.

841
01:09:17.840 --> 01:09:18.875
You have to hurry.

842
01:09:20.560 --> 01:09:21.560
I have a plan.

843
01:09:23.760 --> 01:09:24.988
Hold on!

844
01:09:25.080 --> 01:09:26.957
"Hold on" ain't no goddamn plan!

845
01:09:31.280 --> 01:09:32.554
No, no, no, no!

846
01:09:47.600 --> 01:09:48.669
Hi.

847
01:09:49.440 --> 01:09:51.158
You looking for someone?

848
01:10:00.880 --> 01:10:01.949
That's 200!

849
01:10:22.280 --> 01:10:23.759
Ha-ha! Come on.

850
01:10:29.640 --> 01:10:32.234
No, no, no...
Xander, you got to get to the top floor.

851
01:10:32.320 --> 01:10:33.576
He's trying to engage another satellite.

852
01:10:33.600 --> 01:10:34.600
Hurry.

853
01:10:49.040 --> 01:10:50.314
Fish in a barrel.

854
01:11:04.200 --> 01:11:05.679
Forty-five U.S.P.

855
01:11:06.360 --> 01:11:07.588
Twelve round mag.

856
01:11:09.200 --> 01:11:10.519
Five left.

857
01:11:16.440 --> 01:11:17.440
Three.

858
01:11:32.240 --> 01:11:33.673
What the hell's going on out there?

859
01:11:46.960 --> 01:11:47.960
Empty.

860
01:12:11.920 --> 01:12:14.912
Adele, Xander's in.
Find the target, light him up.

861
01:12:19.080 --> 01:12:20.752
Gibbons thought you'd be back.

862
01:12:21.840 --> 01:12:22.909
To be the hero we needed.

863
01:12:27.080 --> 01:12:30.356
You take the box to the NSA,

864
01:12:30.680 --> 01:12:32.671
and we're right back to
where we started.

865
01:12:36.720 --> 01:12:38.278
Wow.

866
01:12:39.520 --> 01:12:41.351
This is touching.

867
01:12:43.440 --> 01:12:46.238
Gibbons would be proud to
see you two working together.

868
01:12:53.120 --> 01:12:55.634
I'm walking out of here, Xander.

869
01:12:58.360 --> 01:13:00.032
You want to know a secret?

870
01:13:00.720 --> 01:13:02.551
You forgot to put deodorant on?

871
01:13:04.120 --> 01:13:08.033
I killed Gibbons because
he was a self-righteous prick.

872
01:13:08.200 --> 01:13:09.315
Do you have a shot?

873
01:13:09.400 --> 01:13:10.856
He thought
he had the right to police the world.

874
01:13:10.880 --> 01:13:12.360
Adele,
do you have eyes on the target?

875
01:13:13.240 --> 01:13:14.275
I'm switching to thermal.

876
01:13:14.360 --> 01:13:17.750
I was never going to
stop downing satellites

877
01:13:17.880 --> 01:13:20.155
no matter what happened.
You know why?

878
01:13:20.280 --> 01:13:22.999
Because this world has turned...

879
01:13:23.160 --> 01:13:25.435
Please, please, please
tell me you have a shot.

880
01:13:25.520 --> 01:13:26.589
Damn it.

881
01:13:26.680 --> 01:13:29.069
He's turned the heat up. I can't see shit.

882
01:13:29.200 --> 01:13:31.760
X, can't see you guys.
Thermal's no good.

883
01:13:31.840 --> 01:13:33.717
- Right?
- I've lost you in the heat.

884
01:13:33.840 --> 01:13:35.456
You don't see
what's going on in this world?

885
01:13:35.480 --> 01:13:36.480
Take it easy.

886
01:13:36.520 --> 01:13:37.520
Huh?

887
01:13:38.840 --> 01:13:39.976
So, what are you gonna do about it?

888
01:13:40.000 --> 01:13:41.000
Easy.

889
01:13:41.040 --> 01:13:45.238
X, keep Chatty Cathy talking.
I still don't have a shot.

890
01:13:45.320 --> 01:13:47.038
We made it that way.

891
01:13:47.160 --> 01:13:49.355
People like Gibbons and
the two of you. And me.

892
01:13:49.520 --> 01:13:51.556
We made it that way. I mean, come on.

893
01:13:51.880 --> 01:13:53.677
What's the point of getting up
in the morning

894
01:13:53.800 --> 01:13:55.677
if you're not gonna
reboot the world, right?

895
01:13:55.840 --> 01:13:56.875
Okay. Easy.

896
01:13:57.040 --> 01:13:58.376
There's a war out there.

897
01:13:58.400 --> 01:14:00.516
We're at war for our survival,
you don't see it?

898
01:14:00.680 --> 01:14:02.796
Millions of people
have died for nothing...

899
01:14:02.880 --> 01:14:03.880
It's their right.

900
01:14:03.960 --> 01:14:05.712
Read between the lines.

901
01:14:05.840 --> 01:14:07.016
Isn't it right?

902
01:14:07.040 --> 01:14:08.216
I'm gonna be honest with you.

903
01:14:08.240 --> 01:14:10.356
What's been bugging me
this whole time

904
01:14:11.640 --> 01:14:15.269
is you've got something
stuck in between your teeth.

905
01:14:15.400 --> 01:14:16.913
What the hell are you talking about?

906
01:14:17.040 --> 01:14:18.155
I'm serious.

907
01:14:18.240 --> 01:14:20.000
What the hell's wrong with you?

908
01:14:20.400 --> 01:14:21.992
Right there.

909
01:14:23.680 --> 01:14:24.680
Ahh!

910
01:14:28.720 --> 01:14:29.720
Nice shot.

911
01:14:29.840 --> 01:14:31.193
Was there ever a doubt?

912
01:14:31.800 --> 01:14:34.314
Uh, yeah, I confess, I had my doubts.

913
01:14:36.840 --> 01:14:39.832
That's for talking shit
about my friend, Gibbons.

914
01:14:51.320 --> 01:14:54.198
Xiang! Get on your knees!
On your knees!

915
01:14:55.520 --> 01:14:57.511
Hands! Hands!

916
01:14:58.120 --> 01:14:59.394
On your knees, now.

917
01:15:01.320 --> 01:15:02.548
Just in time.

918
01:15:05.600 --> 01:15:07.431
Watch out, Cage. Keep this up,

919
01:15:07.560 --> 01:15:09.520
people might mistake you
for one of the good guys.

920
01:15:12.920 --> 01:15:13.920
Hey, suit.

921
01:15:19.240 --> 01:15:21.037
You got what you wanted.

922
01:15:21.880 --> 01:15:23.240
We both know he's not the bad guy.

923
01:15:23.720 --> 01:15:25.438
And who do we blame for Moscow?

924
01:15:26.080 --> 01:15:29.550
Better a living terrorist
than a dead company man.

925
01:15:29.760 --> 01:15:31.398
You see what I'm saying?

926
01:15:31.480 --> 01:15:32.833
Let's go.

927
01:15:32.960 --> 01:15:35.030
Back on the plane.
I want wheels up in 20.

928
01:15:35.120 --> 01:15:36.120
Let's go, boys.

929
01:15:42.200 --> 01:15:44.350
We recovered Pandora's Box.

930
01:15:44.480 --> 01:15:46.038
They're gonna send an extraction team

931
01:15:46.120 --> 01:15:47.269
to pick you guys up.

932
01:15:47.400 --> 01:15:49.118
But they're taking Xiang.

933
01:15:50.120 --> 01:15:51.838
Oh, and, Serena,

934
01:15:51.960 --> 01:15:55.111
if you don't hear from me,
remember, dial nine.

935
01:15:55.200 --> 01:15:57.236
X takes care of its own.

936
01:15:57.400 --> 01:15:59.356
You gave it back to Marke, didn't you?

937
01:16:09.720 --> 01:16:13.110
Nice place. Spacious. Expensive.

938
01:16:13.240 --> 01:16:14.760
Shut up.

939
01:16:23.560 --> 01:16:25.312
Thank you, sir.

940
01:16:25.400 --> 01:16:28.517
Yes, minimal casualties.
Triple-X performed

941
01:16:28.680 --> 01:16:31.672
beyond any
reasonable measure of expectation.

942
01:16:45.120 --> 01:16:46.758
Let me guess.

943
01:16:48.280 --> 01:16:50.430
That was my invite to the Oval Office.

944
01:16:55.120 --> 01:16:56.439
As of 10 minutes ago,

945
01:16:56.520 --> 01:16:58.590
the Triple-X program
was officially shuttered.

946
01:16:59.200 --> 01:17:01.430
All active agents are to be
erased from record

947
01:17:01.520 --> 01:17:03.351
and considered enemies of the state.

948
01:17:04.960 --> 01:17:08.430
It's just never a good idea
to point a gun at me.

949
01:17:13.280 --> 01:17:15.396
Hey, are NSA extraction teams

950
01:17:15.520 --> 01:17:17.320
normally armed like
they're invading Fallujah?

951
01:17:17.920 --> 01:17:19.672
No, generally not.
Watch the boys.

952
01:17:22.880 --> 01:17:23.880
Shit.

953
01:17:24.480 --> 01:17:26.550
Oh, God, it's happening, isn't it?

954
01:17:26.680 --> 01:17:28.560
They're gonna start
shooting at us, aren't they?

955
01:17:28.600 --> 01:17:30.079
- Come on!
- Clear out, let's go!

956
01:17:31.560 --> 01:17:32.560
It's showtime.

957
01:17:32.640 --> 01:17:34.437
I guess we're on
the same team now.

958
01:17:34.560 --> 01:17:35.913
Give me one.

959
01:17:37.560 --> 01:17:39.835
You know me. Wind me up,

960
01:17:39.920 --> 01:17:41.512
point me in the right direction.

961
01:17:41.640 --> 01:17:43.232
Come on, let's go!

962
01:17:43.360 --> 01:17:45.555
This shit is getting real, isn't it?

963
01:17:45.720 --> 01:17:47.176
Is this what happens
when shit gets real?

964
01:17:47.200 --> 01:17:48.269
What do we do?

965
01:17:48.360 --> 01:17:49.680
Just be where the bullets aren't.

966
01:17:51.320 --> 01:17:54.756
Sadly, the terrorist activated
Pandora's Box

967
01:17:54.840 --> 01:17:57.354
one last time before we could stop him.

968
01:17:57.480 --> 01:17:59.914
You and your entire team were lost

969
01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:02.275
in the blast along with the device itself.

970
01:18:03.160 --> 01:18:06.357
If the world thinks
Pandora's Box is gone,

971
01:18:06.440 --> 01:18:09.159
then they won't know
we're using it to spy on them.

972
01:18:09.280 --> 01:18:11.191
You're just another tyrant.

973
01:18:11.520 --> 01:18:13.476
No. Patriot.

974
01:18:13.600 --> 01:18:15.591
Let me educate you on the difference.

975
01:18:15.720 --> 01:18:17.233
Xander!

976
01:18:19.880 --> 01:18:20.915
Xander!

977
01:18:26.040 --> 01:18:28.713
They say
it's the last great adventure, Cage.

978
01:18:28.800 --> 01:18:30.153
Be sure and send a postcard.

979
01:18:30.280 --> 01:18:31.918
- Engines hot!
- Let's go!

980
01:18:32.000 --> 01:18:33.000
Xander!

981
01:18:33.880 --> 01:18:35.074
Xander Cage!

982
01:18:39.120 --> 01:18:40.917
- Go, go!
- Everybody, fan out!

983
01:18:41.000 --> 01:18:43.116
Find cover! Move!

984
01:18:43.200 --> 01:18:44.428
Get behind there!

985
01:18:46.320 --> 01:18:48.754
- There, take cover! Okay, okay.
- Get behind there!

986
01:19:07.480 --> 01:19:08.913
What a rush.

987
01:19:10.520 --> 01:19:12.636
Damn, Becky, that's some body armor.

988
01:19:17.680 --> 01:19:21.116
Hey. I told you you got no manners.

989
01:19:22.440 --> 01:19:25.000
Did your mother ever teach you
how to zip up your pants?

990
01:19:29.040 --> 01:19:30.040
Shh...

991
01:19:33.000 --> 01:19:34.319
Well?

992
01:19:44.200 --> 01:19:45.200
Serena.

993
01:19:46.120 --> 01:19:47.269
We're a bit busy now!

994
01:19:47.360 --> 01:19:49.032
Marke's got Pandora's Box.

995
01:19:49.160 --> 01:19:51.469
She's gonna drop a satellite
on top of you.

996
01:19:53.080 --> 01:19:54.832
She's gonna drop a satellite on us!

997
01:19:56.680 --> 01:19:58.636
Not if I jam the signal!

998
01:20:01.920 --> 01:20:02.920
I need a power source!

999
01:20:04.520 --> 01:20:05.520
Go!

1000
01:20:05.680 --> 01:20:07.636
Over there? By myself?

1001
01:20:11.440 --> 01:20:12.475
Go!

1002
01:20:13.440 --> 01:20:15.192
Cover me!

1003
01:20:17.240 --> 01:20:18.240
Fan out!

1004
01:20:18.360 --> 01:20:19.395
Go, go!

1005
01:20:21.440 --> 01:20:23.112
Hurry up, over there!

1006
01:20:34.840 --> 01:20:36.159
I go low.

1007
01:20:36.480 --> 01:20:37.833
I'll go high.

1008
01:20:38.360 --> 01:20:40.590
See if I can't find G.I.Joe.

1009
01:21:05.240 --> 01:21:07.231
Are you getting this interference?

1010
01:21:59.840 --> 01:22:01.114
Shit.

1011
01:22:02.880 --> 01:22:03.995
Take 'em out, now!

1012
01:22:11.920 --> 01:22:13.080
Everyone needs backup, right?

1013
01:22:13.840 --> 01:22:15.398
Yeah, I guess.

1014
01:22:51.200 --> 01:22:52.200
Let's do this.

1015
01:23:48.120 --> 01:23:49.439
Nicks!

1016
01:23:50.600 --> 01:23:52.397
- I've got a plan!
- No!

1017
01:23:54.040 --> 01:23:55.632
No, no, no!

1018
01:24:16.880 --> 01:24:19.075
Listen! From now on,
I make the plans, you execute!

1019
01:24:19.240 --> 01:24:20.309
Ow!

1020
01:25:26.520 --> 01:25:28.192
Oh, shit.

1021
01:26:10.400 --> 01:26:13.358
Oh, my God, this is fucking awesome!

1022
01:26:28.040 --> 01:26:30.235
What's wrong, hotshot?
No witty comeback?

1023
01:26:30.320 --> 01:26:33.198
I just finally figured out
that math problem.

1024
01:26:46.880 --> 01:26:49.235
It's gonna take two flushes.

1025
01:26:53.600 --> 01:26:54.600
Go, go, go!

1026
01:26:56.520 --> 01:26:58.795
Oh, shit. Way too many.
Let's get out of here.

1027
01:27:00.960 --> 01:27:02.029
Get back! Come on!

1028
01:27:02.720 --> 01:27:03.720
Oh, shit!

1029
01:27:05.400 --> 01:27:06.879
Oh, my, God, I'm gonna die.

1030
01:27:13.320 --> 01:27:14.070
Move!

1031
01:27:14.160 --> 01:27:15.673
Push forward!

1032
01:27:17.920 --> 01:27:19.478
This is all we've got.

1033
01:27:19.800 --> 01:27:21.199
Pin 'em! Pin 'em down!

1034
01:27:22.400 --> 01:27:24.630
Damn! I'm out of bullets. You got any?

1035
01:27:25.200 --> 01:27:26.838
No. Nothing.

1036
01:27:29.120 --> 01:27:30.155
I'm empty.

1037
01:27:34.600 --> 01:27:36.591
- We go on three.
- Okay.

1038
01:28:18.640 --> 01:28:19.640
Wassup?

1039
01:28:21.760 --> 01:28:26.197
Rock, paper, scissor, grenade launcher.

1040
01:28:28.280 --> 01:28:29.554
Darius Stone.

1041
01:28:36.320 --> 01:28:38.834
Triple-X since 2005.

1042
01:28:39.000 --> 01:28:40.558
Thanks for the assist.

1043
01:28:40.720 --> 01:28:42.551
X takes care of its own.

1044
01:29:14.160 --> 01:29:15.752
You got to be kidding.

1045
01:29:49.080 --> 01:29:50.433
We failed.

1046
01:29:55.840 --> 01:29:59.549
Xander, Marke activated
the satellite and it's headed right for us.

1047
01:29:59.640 --> 01:30:01.790
I'm gonna have to
take it out kamikaze style.

1048
01:30:01.920 --> 01:30:05.230
Don't do it. It's suicide.
Nobody could survive that fall.

1049
01:30:05.360 --> 01:30:07.920
Tell Nicks to have that camera ready.

1050
01:30:08.000 --> 01:30:10.992
Low-orbit freefall,
no chute and big fireworks.

1051
01:30:17.200 --> 01:30:19.475
They say it's the last great adventure.

1052
01:30:32.000 --> 01:30:33.956
Be sure to send a postcard.

1053
